          "issue": "In this English construction, “all the same” is concessive, meaning “nevertheless.” The supplied ὁμῶς ordinarily expresses likeness or equality, whereas the familiar concessive adverb is ὅμως. The note lists “alike” and “all the same” without distinguishing the English phrase's concessive force or explaining a supported concessive interpretation of the supplied spelling. Its appeal to irony does not by itself establish that lexical shift. This is an interpretive issue with verified print, not evidence of an OCR defect.",
